    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi,<div><br></div><div>It seems the error is being thrown at this step in <font face=\"courier new, monospace\">correctReadDepth</font></div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><div> targetIR &lt;- RangedData(ranges = IRanges(start = targetedSequence[, 2],</div><div>                        end = targetedSequence[, 3]), space = targetedSequence[, 1])</div></div></code></div><br>Can you make sure that the exons data frame is well-formed and that it has 3 columns?</div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><font color=\"#660066\">ncol(exons) # should give 3 </font></div></code></div><br>Also, make sure that you are using the UCSC chromosome naming convention because you have &quot;chr&quot; in the chromosome.</div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">genomeStyle</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;UCSC&quot;</span></div></code></div><br></div><div>Please let me know if this helps.</div><div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div>Gavin</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
